<title>TURKEY: Turkish Otosan Q1 profits jump 215 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish Otosan Q1 profits jump 215 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 2,606.29 vs     872.62</p>
<p>    Net profit		  3,629.26 vs   1,151.86</p>
<p>    Net sales		  18,438.36 vs   5,806.17</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  3,459.02 vs   1,453.55</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	2,254.80 vs     483.56</p>
<p>    Interest paid		   3.01 vs	 1.58</p>
<p>    Total debts		20,993.34 vs   6,037.04</p>
<p>    Equity		     13,708.19 vs   5,225.01</p>
<p>    Capital		     1,392.50 vs   1,320.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkish passenger car and commercial vehicle producer Otosan Otomobil Sanayii A.S. is owned 53.6 percent by Turkey's leading industrial Koc group and Koc family and 28.4 percent by Ford Motor Co.</p>
<p>The partners agreed late last year to equalise their equity stakes in Otosan after Otosan's founder shares are cancelled and its marketing arm Otosan Pazarlama is merged into Otosan.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
